* text=auto
*.cs text
*.ts text
*.json text
*.md text

# Git hooks MUST be LF. `core.autocrlf=true` is set on this machine, so without this line the checked-out
# .githooks/pre-commit gets CRLF, `#!/bin/sh` becomes `/bin/sh\r`, and the hook dies with "bad interpreter"
# on every commit. That failure looks like the hook being broken rather than the register being checked, and
# a hook that errors for an unrelated reason is worse than no hook: people delete it.
.githooks/* text eol=lf

# The assistant pack records content hashes, so its installed bytes must match on every platform.
Semanticus.VSCode/assistant-pack/** text eol=lf

# Workflow definitions are pinned by a hash of their bytes (LocalEngine.Workflows.cs WorkflowRevision), and the
# v1.1.3 compatibility copies must stay byte-exact to the baseline on every platform. A CRLF checkout would change
# every hash and fail Shipped_v1_1_3_compatibility_files_are_byte_exact on Windows.
Semanticus.Engine/workflows/** text eol=lf
Semanticus.Engine/workflows-compat/** text eol=lf
# The frozen v7 fixture is compared byte-wise with its own rename; keep it LF like the shipped workflows.
Semanticus.Tests/fixtures/verified-measure-frozen/** text eol=lf
